<title>BRAZIL: Brazil 12-mo current account deficit 3.9 pct/GDP.</title>
<headline>Brazil 12-mo current account deficit 3.9 pct/GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's current account deficit reached $29.888 billion in the 12 months ending in April, equivalent to 3.9 percent of gross domestic product, a Central Bank official said.</p>
<p>Altamir Lopes, head of the Central Bank's economics department, told reporters the 12-month deficit to the end of March had been $27.733 billion, or 3.63 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>The current account deficit in the month of April totaled $3.906 billion, he said.</p>
<p>(( -- James Craig, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
